From: apxchol benchmark harness <adamant.pwn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] experiment/driver: run the solve at any thread count, and let
 the PCG tolerance be configured

Two hard-coded assumptions in the CPU experiment driver keep it from being
benchmarked at a chosen tolerance on a machine that is not a 32-core Perlmutter
node. Neither changes any numerics.

1. `if(num_threads == 32)` gates the entire PCG solve. Run the driver with any
   other thread count and it factorizes and then exits without solving, so there
   is no iteration count and no residual to report.

2. `example_pcg_solver` already takes `max_iter` and `rel_tol` as parameters, but
   the call site never passes them, so they are pinned at 1000 / 1e-7. Its two
   sibling entry points already expose them: `experiment/independent_cg.cpp`
   reads both from argv (argv[4], argv[5]) and the CUDA drivers take the
   tolerance as argv[4]. Reading them from the environment here keeps the
   driver's positional-argument convention intact (argv[4] already selects
   physics mode) while making the tolerance configurable. Defaults are unchanged.

The stopping test itself is untouched. Note for anyone calibrating it: the test
is `sqrt(dpar[4]) > sqrt(dpar[0])`, i.e. it compares the residual norm against
sqrt(rel_tol) and is therefore an ABSOLUTE test -- at the default 1e-7 it stops
at ||r|| <= 3.16e-4 regardless of ||b||.

---
--- a/experiment/driver_local.cpp
+++ b/experiment/driver_local.cpp
@@ -1,10 +1,11 @@
 
 
 //#include <mpi.h>
 #include <chrono>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include "custom_cg.hpp"
 #include <atomic>
 
 
 typedef int custom_idx;
 
@@ -1027,15 +1028,24 @@
     printf("triangular solve max path: %d at index: %d\n", *max_path, std::distance(max_path_dp.begin(), max_path));
   
     
 
     custom_space::sparse_matrix<type_int, type_data> precond_M(processor.mat.rows(), processor.mat.cols(), std::move(csr_val_host), std::move(csr_col_ind_host), std::move(csr_rowptr_host));
 
-    if(num_threads == 32)
-    {
-       example_pcg_solver(processor.mat, precond_M, diagonal_entries.data(), is_graph);
+    if(num_threads >= 1)
+    {
+       // The PCG parameters are already parameters of example_pcg_solver; they were
+       // just never passed. Read them from the environment (as independent_cg.cpp
+       // takes them on argv and the CUDA drivers take the tolerance as argv[4]), so
+       // a benchmark can request a tolerance without editing the source. Defaults
+       // are unchanged.
+       const char *env_iter = getenv("PARAC_MAX_ITER");
+       const char *env_tol  = getenv("PARAC_REL_TOL");
+       example_pcg_solver(processor.mat, precond_M, diagonal_entries.data(), is_graph,
+                          env_iter ? atoi(env_iter) : 1000,
+                          env_tol  ? atof(env_tol)  : 1e-7);
     }
     
     for(int li = 0; li < 10; li++)
     {
         printf("\n");
     }
